  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "The vertices of a \\(3\\)–\\(4\\)–\\(5\\) right triangle are the centers of three mutually externally tangent circles, as shown. What is the sum of the areas of these circles?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(12\\pi\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{25\\pi}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(13\\pi\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{27\\pi}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(14\\pi\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2006-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(r, s, t\\) are the radii at the vertices, then \\(r + s = 3,\\ r + t = 4,\\ s + t = 5.\\) Adding all three gives \\(r + s + t = 6,\\) so \\(r = 1,\\ s = 2,\\ t = 3.\\)\n\nThe sum of the areas is \\(\\pi(1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2) = 14\\pi.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "The radii at two adjacent vertices sum to the side length between them",
        "Solve \\(r + s = 3,\\ r + t = 4,\\ s + t = 5\\)"
      ],
